From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:12:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ec/lenovo/h8: Return the battery strings of _BIF and _BIX as
 strings

ACPI defines Model Number, Serial Number, Battery Type and OEM
Information of _BIF and _BIX as strings. BINX() puts buffers there: the
128-bit EC fields BANA and BAOE as they read, and the serial number and
type in buffers built in the method. Linux takes a buffer in those
places too; an OS that goes by the specification need not.

Convert each with ToString(), up to its first NUL. BINF() copies the
four from the _BIX package, so _BIF gets strings as well.

TEST=Built lenovo/w541 with mrc.bin and with the native RAM init. In
acpiexec (ACPICA 20230628), _BIX of BAT0 returns strings at indices 16
to 19; before, ACPICA repaired the package and logged "Converted
Buffer to expected String" for each of the four.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/battery.asl | 13 +++++++++----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/battery.asl b/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/battery.asl
index 0560a3ba2d..c15b7bb516 100644
--- a/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/battery.asl
+++ b/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/battery.asl
@@ -207,6 +207,9 @@ Method(BINF, 3, Serialized)
  *
  * Arg0: Template with default values
  * Arg1: Battery ID (0x1=BAT0; 0x2=BAT1)
+ *
+ * The EC keeps model, serial number, type and OEM name as bytes: they go
+ * into the package as strings, the type that ACPI gives these fields.
  */
 Method(BINX, 2, Serialized)
 {
@@ -256,21 +259,23 @@ Method(BINX, 2, Serialized)
 		SERN [Local1] = Local2 + 48
 		Local1--
 	}
-	Arg0 [0x11] = SERN
+	Arg0 [0x11] = ToString (SERN, Ones)
 
 	// Battery Type
 	^BPAG(Arg1 | 4)
 	Name (TYPE, Buffer() { 0, 0, 0, 0, 0 })
 	TYPE = BATY
-	Arg0 [0x12] = TYPE
+	Arg0 [0x12] = ToString (TYPE, Ones)
 
 	// OEM Information
 	^BPAG(Arg1 | 5)
-	Arg0 [0x13] = BAOE
+	Local0 = BAOE
+	Arg0 [0x13] = ToString (Local0, Ones)
 
 	// Model Number
 	^BPAG(Arg1 | 6)
-	Arg0 [0x10] = BANA
+	Local0 = BANA
+	Arg0 [0x10] = ToString (Local0, Ones)
 
 	Release(ECLK)
 	Return (Arg0)
